+# N23 native UUID object correction — second prospective engineering exception
+
+Recorded 2026-09-30 before any execution of corrected native-object code. This is a transparent extension of necessary engineering work under the continuing explicit autonomous research instruction, interpreted by the coordinator; it is not new user approval, a budget expansion, an algorithm variant, or a retrospective valid result.
+
+## Two exhausted opportunities
+
+The original backend attempt `rdt-qd-ed-final-20260921T093925Z__n23_backend_preflight_v2__7ca117f9b7fb` (source `77302aab40d6b059e85c8d1d8011ea36cb3d3856`, 6.538148973020725 GPU-process seconds) failed before arithmetic because of its UUID check. Original root review `backend-failure-review-v1.json` SHA256 `95353cd515ca1e759e781d63108ecf03fcdea62372c7d1578159fe79a225c661` remains immutable.
+
+The separately authorized first engineering recovery `rdt-qd-ed-final-20260921T093925Z__n23_backend_uuid_repair__41eab61a8079` (source `675c2f4d07e787a7e160a2a26312c8ab2e4a19f6`, 6.601666689035483 GPU-process seconds) also failed before arithmetic. Its root review `uuid-repair-native-type-failure-review-v1.json` SHA256 `b6bed05adae2e1895a17bb331bfa91f6176eb37591bad02ff807958245bd72a7` binds its complete plan/report/terminal and prior failure. The first exception `uuid-repair-engineering-exception-v1.md` SHA256 `d5c80006512203343d89dc24ab4de53356c045bc0f755800bf0e8337524d5f20` is exhausted and permits no further run. All its files and authority records are preserved.
+
+Both reports have accepted=false, task_outcome=false, empty batches/synthetic lists and exactly `RuntimeError:audit physical CUDA UUID differs or unavailable`. Both ledger groups must remain reserved/dispatched/aborted, with complete original costs and explicit second retry_of first. Neither report retained the actual live UUID. No N23 Dev reservation or task outcome exists.
+
+## Concrete correction and evidence boundary
+
+The installed PyTorch2.7.1+cu126 exposes a non-string `torch._C._CUuuid` class. The [official v2.7.1 binding](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pytorch/pytorch/v2.7.1/torch/csrc/cuda/Module.cpp), lines991–999 and1038–1039, exposes the native object, a16-byte value and its string representation. The first repair dropped the old str conversion and tested only string fixtures, so it rejected this legitimate native type. This is an independently identified software defect. It does not establish the failed workers' actual physical-device value.
+
+Before release, the executor must CPU-test support for strings or the installed exact native UUID type, validate byte/string agreement, retain JSON-safe serialized raw/type/canonical identity, reject malformed/mismatched/arbitrary objects and preserve all visible-device/count/current-device checks. Failure reports must retain bounded public identity diagnostics. No credential contents or environment values outside device identity are recorded. Complete frozen source review must cover these changes and their narrowly necessary admission/proof/tests. All science, model, Stage, provider, profiles, arithmetic, tolerance, corpus and task conditions remain byte-identical to source77302aab. Existing v1 protocols and results are not rewritten.
+
+## One additional metered backend attempt
+
+This new exception prospectively allows exactly one additional backend execution after the concrete CPU correction and root review: at most three backend attempts total, explicitly preserving both failed predecessors. A new attempt must identify retry_of the second failure and transitively retain the first. A different predecessor, any additional backend reservation, any N23 Dev reservation before the repaired proof, any arithmetic already evaluated in a failed predecessor, an unresolved attempt, or altered evidence blocks this exception.
+
+Use new versioned exception/authority/source-review/frozen-plan paths. Never overwrite previous reviews/plans. The active authority must be adopted under the private runner/state locks and bound by hash to the exact final source and runtime. No generic retry switch or renamed scientific cohort. The original N23 v2 four-arm Dev matrix stays the only conditional scientific target.
+
+Use one exclusive idle GPU7 process with the same frozen UUID/EGL/runtime and accounted health probe. Charge one existing recovery slot, at most120 seconds plus40 seconds cleanup, before dispatch. Keep cumulative478 attempts/100 GPU-hours, buckets51/187/180/40/20 and protected32/12-hour reservations unchanged. Require the full remaining22-hour Dev ceiling, both Dev timeout recovery slots and protected reserves to fit. Both old failures remain charged. No model/provider/simulator call is permitted in this backend test.
+
+Replay exactly the original176 canonical batches/2816 candidates from the same2250 saved N21 task0 bundles, and the same two synthetic FP32/BF16 batches. All exact arithmetic and wrong-bound rejection checks remain unchanged. No tolerance adjustment, failed-prefix omission or outcome-based selection. Any error, timeout, mismatch or incomplete proof closes this exception; it grants no fourth backend execution.
+
+## Conditional Dev continuation
+
+Only the complete valid third-attempt proof, with raw/type/canonical CUDA evidence, all three ledger groups and exactly the final Dev source/runtime, may unlock the unchanged N23 v2 Dev plan. Preserve original main/cohort/arms/task order/seeds/limits/timeout-recovery policy and promotion rules; add this exception and all backend lineage to provenance. Protected validation/formal remain closed until original scientific gates.
+
+Stage uses only the current Codex managed login. Poe and other provider fallbacks remain disabled; saved Poe credentials are preserved. CPU implementation is authorized now; this document does not launch a GPU worker. Concrete source/runtime review, exact named failure proof, actual capacity, locked authority adoption and a fresh immutable plan are required before the one added execution.
